The proto contract lands in M0b (branch feat/proto-contract).

This file is a one-time bootstrap token, not a condition.

`make typecheck-proto` and `make generate` refuse to run buf while it exists,
because buf errors on a module with no .proto files. Deleting it is a required
checklist item of the M0b PR — and the Makefile HARD-FAILS if any .proto file
exists while this file is still here, so the bootstrap cannot outlive its
purpose.

This shape was chosen over `if [ -d proto ]` deliberately. Phase-1 review
finding A8: a directory-presence test is re-evaluable, so any future merge that
emptied or renamed proto/ would silently re-disable breaking-change protection
on the repo's most covenant-critical gate. A tracked file cannot be
resurrected by a rename.

See docs/plans/2026-08-18-repo-foundation.md.
